    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to Read This",
      "items": [
        "Lines show ownership and data direction; detailed command names stay in nodes and cards to avoid label overlap.",
        "The shared layer validates typed contracts, enforces policy/session scope, then routes by platform and capability.",
        "The current code constant lists 66 MCP tools; the diagram groups them by implementation path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Android Backend",
      "items": [
        "UI tools use UIAutomator hierarchy first, then ADB input commands for tap, type, back, and swipe.",
        "Lifecycle and device tools use ADB install, monkey launch, force-stop, pm clear, and adb devices.",
        "Diagnostics use screencap, logcat, crash buffers, ANR traces, bugreport, screenrecord, and Perfetto."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "iOS Backend",
      "items": [
        "The iOS router auto-selects AXe for simulators and WDA for physical devices unless overridden.",
        "simctl and devicectl provide lifecycle, install, launch, log, crash, and attach-target support.",
        "xctrace templates and WDA/AXe artifacts feed the same ToolResult and artifact pipeline."
      ]
    }
